<Base title="Privacy" description="Privacy policy for Bump Compass — what we collect, what we don't, and why. Written for readers in the EU, UK, Switzerland and the United States.">
  <section class="section section-white">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p><em>Last updated: 14 October 2026</em></p>

    <h2 id="short">The short version</h2>

    <p>Our calculators run entirely in your browser. Your dates, weights and cycle lengths are never sent to us — there is no server to send them to.</p>

    <p>We collect an email address only when you ask us for something (like the free PDF), and an optional due date if you choose to give one. We use Google AdSense to display advertising on our public pages. That is the whole picture, and the rest of this page is the detail.</p>

    <p><strong>We never sell your personal information. We never use your pregnancy information to target advertising at you.</strong></p>

    <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>

    <p>Bump Compass ("we", "us") publishes free pregnancy calculators and guides at <a href="https://bumpcompass.com/">bumpcompass.com</a>. For the purposes of the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), we are the <strong>data controller</strong> for the personal information described in this policy.</p>

    <p>You can reach us at <a href="/contact/">contact@bumpcompass.com</a> for any privacy question, including requests to exercise the rights set out below.</p>

    <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>

    <h3>Information you give us</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your email address</strong> — when you request a free PDF or subscribe to our emails.</li>
      <li><strong>An optional due date or week of pregnancy</strong> — only if you choose to enter it on the download form. This field is voluntary and the form works without it.</li>
      <li><strong>The contents of any message you send us</strong>, and your email address, if you write to us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Standard server logs</strong> — our hosting provider, Cloudflare, records technical information such as IP address, browser type and the pages requested. This is used for security, abuse prevention and keeping the site online.</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising cookies</strong> set by Google and its partners, described under <a href="#ads">Advertising and cookies</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What we do not collect</h3>

    <ul>
      <li>We do not store your calculator inputs. They are processed in your browser and never transmitted to us.</li>
      <li>We do not run analytics or behavioural tracking scripts of our own.</li>
      <li>We do not build advertising profiles, and we do not buy or receive data about you from data brokers.</li>
      <li>We do not ask for your name, address, phone number or payment details. We have no accounts and take no payments today.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="email">Email, the free PDF and our newsletter</h2>

    <p>When you request a free PDF, we ask for your email address and, optionally, your due date or week of pregnancy. We use that email address to:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>send you the PDF you asked for;</li>
      <li>ask you to confirm your subscription (a confirmation email — see below); and</li>
      <li>send you occasional emails about pregnancy and about Bump Compass, if you confirm.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>If you give us a due date, we use it to send you information relevant to your stage of pregnancy, and to stop sending stage-specific emails once that stage has passed.</p>

    <p><strong>Confirmation first.</strong> We use a double opt-in process. After you submit the form, we send you a confirmation email. You are only added to our mailing list once you click the link in it. If you never confirm, we do not email you again.</p>

    <p><strong>Who sends it.</strong> Our emails are delivered through <strong>MailerLite</strong> (MailerLite UAB, Paupio str. 46, Vilnius, Lithuania, company number 302942057), which acts as our data processor under a Data Processing Agreement. MailerLite is headquartered in the European Union and stores data on EU infrastructure.</p>

    <p><strong>Unsubscribing.</strong> Every email we send contains a one-click unsubscribe link. You can also ask us to delete your data entirely by writing to <a href="/contact/">contact@bumpcompass.com</a>. Unsubscribing does not affect your use of any tool on this site.</p>

    <p><strong>Never sold or shared.</strong> We do not sell, rent or share your email address with anyone for their own marketing. It is used to send you what you asked for, and nothing else.</p>

    <h2 id="ads">Advertising and cookies</h2>

    <p>We display advertising on our public pages through Google AdSense.</p>

    <p>Third party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visit to this site and/or other sites on the Internet. You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>. Alternatively, you can opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalised advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">www.aboutads.info</a>.</p>

    <p>Ads on our public pages are matched to the <em>subject of the page</em> — for example, a page about weight gain shows ads about pregnancy — not to you as an individual. <strong>We do not use your pregnancy or health information to target advertising at you, and we do not display advertising on pages where you are signed in.</strong> (There are no accounts today; this is a commitment we are making in advance of launching them.)</p>

    <h3>If you are in the EEA, the UK or Switzerland</h3>

    <p>We ask for your consent before advertising cookies are used, through a consent message provided by Google's certified consent management platform (CMP). The message lets you accept, refuse, or choose specific purposes and vendors, and it lists the advertising partners involved. Your choice is recorded so we can demonstrate it, and you can change or withdraw it at any time by reopening the consent message.</p>

    <p>Refusing advertising cookies does not restrict any tool or content on this site. It only means you will see non-personalised ads.</p>

    <h3>Controlling cookies</h3>

    <p>You can also block or delete cookies through your browser settings. Blocking advertising cookies does not stop you using any calculator, guide or download on this site. How Google uses information from sites that use its services is described at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.</p>

    <h3>Third-party advertising vendors</h3>

    <p>Google and the advertising partners it works with may collect or receive information as a consequence of ads served on this site. We do not control those parties, and each is responsible for its own privacy practices. You can review the current list of advertising technology partners and their privacy policies in Google's help centre at <a href="https://support.google.com/adsense/answer/9012903" rel="noopener">Ad technology partners</a>, and opt out of many of them at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a> or <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="noopener">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="bases">Our legal bases for processing</h2>

    <p>Where the GDPR applies, we rely on the following legal bases:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Consent</strong> (Article 6(1)(a)) — for sending you emails, for advertising cookies in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland, and for storing any health information you choose to give us.</li>
      <li><strong>Explicit consent</strong> (Article 9(2)(a)) — for any health information you choose to provide, such as a due date or week of pregnancy. This is a special category of data and is treated separately, as explained below.</li>
      <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> (Article 6(1)(f)) — for keeping the site secure and available, for preventing abuse, and for replying to messages you send us. We have balanced these interests against your rights and consider the impact on you to be minimal.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>We keep a record of the consent you give us — what you agreed to and when — so that we can demonstrate it if asked. You can withdraw consent at any time, and withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of anything done before it.</p>

    <h2 id="health">Health information</h2>

    <p><strong>Information about pregnancy is "data concerning health" under Article 9 of the GDPR</strong>, which is a special category of personal data. Processing it requires a higher standard of consent than ordinary personal data.</p>

    <p>This matters in two places on our site:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>The optional due date field</strong> on the download form. If you fill it in, you are giving us health information. We ask for it separately from everything else, it is genuinely optional, and we use it only to make the emails we send you relevant to your stage of pregnancy.</li>
      <li><strong>Our calculators</strong> do not transmit anything, so no health information reaches us from them at all.</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Accepting cookies is never treated as agreement to store your health information.</strong> These are different consents for different purposes, and we do not bundle them. Refusing advertising cookies does not affect our ability to send you a PDF, and declining to give a due date does not restrict any tool on this site.</p>

    <p>We store as little health information as possible: a due date or week, only if you volunteer it. We do not infer, derive or enrich it.</p>

    <h2 id="never">What we will never do</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>We will never sell your personal information.</li>
      <li>We will never use your pregnancy or health information to target advertising at you.</li>
      <li>We will never share your health information with advertisers or data brokers.</li>
      <li>We will never display advertising on pages where you are signed in.</li>
      <li>We will never ask you to agree to store health information as a condition of using a free tool.</li>
      <li>We will never treat silence, inactivity or a pre-ticked box as your consent.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="retention">How long we keep things</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Calculator inputs</strong> — never transmitted, so nothing is retained.</li>
      <li><strong>Emails you send us</strong> — kept only as long as needed to answer them, then deleted.</li>
      <li><strong>Newsletter subscription</strong> — kept until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it. If you never confirm your subscription, your address is removed.</li>
      <li><strong>A due date, if you gave one</strong> — kept alongside your subscription, and deleted when you unsubscribe or ask us to.</li>
      <li><strong>Server logs</strong> — retained by our hosting provider for a short period for security purposes, then discarded.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="rights-eu">Your rights — EEA, UK and Switzerland</h2>

    <p>If the GDPR applies to you, you have the right to:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal information we hold about you;</li>
      <li><strong>Correct</strong> anything inaccurate;</li>
      <li><strong>Delete</strong> it ("the right to be forgotten");</li>
      <li><strong>Restrict</strong> how we use it;</li>
      <li><strong>Object</strong> to our processing, including processing based on legitimate interests;</li>
      <li><strong>Portability</strong> — receive a copy of what you gave us in a machine-readable format;</li>
      <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time; and</li>
      <li><strong>Complain</strong> to your national data protection authority.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>To exercise any of these, write to <a href="/contact/">contact@bumpcompass.com</a>. We will respond within one month. There is no charge, and exercising your rights will never affect your access to any tool on this site.</p>

    <h2 id="rights-us">Your rights — United States</h2>

    <p>If you are a resident of California, you have rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (CCPA/CPRA). Residents of other US states with comprehensive privacy laws (including Virginia, Colorado, Connecticut, Utah and Texas) have similar rights. These include the right to:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Know</strong> what categories of personal information we collect and how we use it;</li>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</li>
      <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate personal information;</li>
      <li><strong>Delete</strong> personal information we have collected from you;</li>
      <li><strong>Opt out</strong> of the "sale" or "sharing" of personal information, and of targeted advertising;</li>
      <li><strong>Limit</strong> the use of sensitive personal information; and</li>
      <li><strong>Not be discriminated against</strong> for exercising any of these rights.</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>We do not sell personal information</strong> in the ordinary sense — we do not exchange it for money. However, under the CCPA/CPRA, using cookies to show you personalised advertising can count as "sharing" personal information for cross-context behavioural advertising, and as processing for targeted advertising under other state laws. You can opt out of this by:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>using the consent message shown on the site, if you are shown one;</li>
      <li>opting out of personalised advertising at <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>; or</li>
      <li>writing to <a href="/contact/">contact@bumpcompass.com</a> and asking us to stop.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>We do not knowingly collect, sell or share the personal information of consumers under 16 years of age. To exercise any US privacy right, write to <a href="/contact/">contact@bumpcompass.com</a>. We will verify your request using the email address you contacted us from, and respond within the timeframe required by the applicable law.</p>

    <h2 id="transfers">International transfers</h2>

    <p>Our site and its logs are hosted by <strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong>, a United States company, which may process data outside the EEA or the UK. Transfers rely on the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses or an equivalent safeguard, under Cloudflare's Data Processing Agreement. Cloudflare has committed to notifying us of legal requests for customer data before disclosure, unless legally barred from doing so.</p>

    <p>Our email list is held by <strong>MailerLite</strong>, which is established in the European Union, so no third-country transfer arises for that processing.</p>

    <h2 id="law">Law enforcement</h2>

    <p>We do not voluntarily provide personal information to law enforcement. If we receive a legally binding request, we will disclose only what the law compels, and we will notify the person affected unless we are legally prohibited from doing so.</p>

    <h2 id="children">Children</h2>

    <p>This site is written for adults and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 16. If you believe a child has given us personal information, write to <a href="/contact/">contact@bumpcompass.com</a> and we will delete it.</p>

    <h2 id="links">Third-party links</h2>

    <p>Our guides may link to other websites, including through affiliate links. When you follow one, that site may collect information about you under its own privacy policy. We are not responsible for those practices and encourage you to read the policy of any site you visit. Our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> explains how those links work and confirms that our clinical content is unaffected by any commercial relationship.</p>

    <h2 id="coming">What is coming: accounts and an app</h2>

    <p><em>This section describes features we plan to launch. It is here now so you can see our intentions before they exist, and so you can hold us to them. When these features launch we will update this page and ask for your consent before storing anything.</em></p>

    <p>We plan to offer optional accounts and a companion app that can store your pregnancy information — such as your due date, your week, and any tracking you choose to enter — so it is available when you come back, on any device. We plan to use accounts to offer paid guides and ebooks.</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Optional.</strong> Every tool on this site will keep working without an account.</li>

      <li><strong>Your explicit consent, asked separately.</strong> Pregnancy information is health information. We will ask for your explicit consent to store it, separately from any cookie choice and separately from our terms. Accepting cookies will never be treated as agreement to store your health information.</li>

      <li><strong>You can withdraw and delete.</strong> You will be able to withdraw that consent at any time and delete your account and everything in it, permanently. We will not keep a copy.</li>

      <li><strong>You can download everything.</strong> You will be able to export a copy of everything we hold about you, at any time, from your account.</li>

      <li><strong>No advertising where you are signed in.</strong> We do not display advertising on pages where you are logged in, and we never use your pregnancy or health information to target advertising anywhere.</li>

      <li><strong>Minimal by design.</strong> We will store only what you choose to enter, and nothing we do not need.</li>

      <li><strong>Encrypted</strong> in transit and at rest.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>We will complete a data protection impact assessment before these features launch, and we will publish what it concludes.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>

    <p>We may update this policy. Changes are posted on this page with a new revision date, and material changes will be communicated by email to subscribers. Previous versions are available on request.</p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>

    <p>Questions about this policy, or any request to exercise a right described above: <a href="/contact/">contact@bumpcompass.com</a>.</p>

    <p><em>This policy is not legal advice to anyone reading it, and it does not create rights beyond those the applicable law provides.</em></p>
